{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Draw near.</b> These are the words of the prophet." "<b>Not from the beginning, etc.</b> From the first I did not speak this sod and this decree in secret." "<b>From the time that it was, etc.</b> The Gaon [Saadia] said: from here is a hint that the soul precedes the body. But he said nothing, for Scripture says at the beginning, 'now they were created' and not 'from of old.' The meaning is: when this decree that went forth from the mouth of HaShem was decreed, to the angels — they are the princes appointed over the kingdoms — as is written in the book of Daniel (Daniel 10:20), 'there I was also.'" "<b>And His spirit</b> is the angel. The Gaon [Saadia] said that the vav is in place of a bet, and said that they interpreted similarly 'they sought YHWH and His strength' (Psalms 105:4). And there is no need [for this]."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 48, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:37.253604374Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}